  "question": {
    "text": "The two circles <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> touch each other, if <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "None of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The two circles touch each other internally as shown in the figure below</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0093_32e0d0ab7876.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.60694in;height:2.51389in\" /></p><p>For the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the centre&nbsp;is at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and radius is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;units.</p><p>Also, the circle is passing through the origin.</p><p>For the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>,&nbsp;the centre is at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and radius is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;units&nbsp;</p><p>From the figure,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>a</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>"
  }
}